  "verdict": "does not separate. The hazardous leaks compress dReading/dT_true to 0.08-0.77 at a 250 degC reading; the identified a spans 6.8x over the three modelled frying pans with eta and food alone (the prior bounds 100x), so a leak looks like a heavier pan. Holding a pan at 300 instead of 250 degC costs 1.21-1.41x the power; the honest 250 degC hold power already spans 1.67x over three modelled pans (real pan sizes spread it further) and the firmware has only commanded power with eta unknown (0.82-0.92). The rim follows the pan with a weight of 0.65-0.96, a wider spread than the compression of the leaks that matter (0.77 at 1.73 kohm)."
